  "preamble": "Merger of the retroflex approximant [ɻ] with the retroflex lateral [ɭ]. Proto-Dravidian had a retroflex approximant *ɻ (ḻ, Wiktionary ẓ), still kept in Tamil and Malayalam. In Kannada it was preserved in Old Kannada, written ೞ, and then merged with ḷ, so Old Kannada kōḻi 'hen' is modern kōḷi. Kodava shows the same merger.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Lateralization, Merger",
